Subject: [PATCH] mmc: no retuning after ungating the clock, as on Loire

Qualcomm's tree asks for the SD controller's tuning to be redone each time its
clock is ungated. Sony switched that off for the Xperia X, the same SoC and
the same controllers; the Z500KL is given the same behaviour.
---
--- drivers/mmc/core/core.c
+++ drivers/mmc/core/core.c
@@ -2579,7 +2579,7 @@ void mmc_ungate_clock(struct mmc_host *host)
 		WARN_ON(host->ios.clock);
 		/* This call will also set host->clk_gated to false */
 		__mmc_set_clock(host, host->clk_old);
-#ifndef CONFIG_ARCH_SONY_LOIRE
+#if !defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SONY_LOIRE) && !defined(CONFIG_MACH_ASUS_Z500KL)
 		/*
 		 * We have seen that host controller's clock tuning circuit may
 		 * go out of sync if controller clocks are gated.
